ype for relationships which refer to classes found later in the same file.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nIt should be able to set the correct type. To be honest I'm not sure if this is a bug in the plugin, or a limitation in mypy's plugin system. Or simply a yet-to-be-implemented feature.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nDefault mypy settings, `mypy.ini` contains only the line to enable sqlalchemy's plugin.\r\n```python\r\nfrom typing import List, Optional\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, Integer, String, ForeignKey\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Mapped, declarative_base, relationship\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\nclass User(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'user'\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    name = Column(String)\r\n\r\n    addresses: List[\"Address\"] = relationship(\"Address\", back_populates=\"user\")\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def some_property(self) -> List[Optional[int]]:\r\n        return [i.id for i in self.addresses]\r\n\r\nclass Address(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'address'\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    user_id: int = Column(ForeignKey(\"user.id\"))\r\n\r\n    user: \"User\" = relationship(\"User\", back_populates=\"addresses\")\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def some_other_property(self) -> Optional[str]:\r\n        return self.user.name\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Error**\r\n\r\n```\r\nfoo.py:17: error: \"List?[Address?]\" has no attribute \"__iter__\" (not iterable)\r\nFound 1 error in 1 file (checked 1 source file)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSwapping the positions of the two classes the error above goes away, but it gets replaced by this (line 17 here refers to the last line of the snippet above):\r\n```\r\nbar.py:17: error: User? has no attribute \"name\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Versions.**\r\n - OS: Debian 10\r\n - Python: 3.7.10, 3.9.4, 3.8.9\r\n - SQLAlchemy: 1.4.7\r\n - sqlalchemy2-stubs: 0.0.1a4\r\n - mypy: 0.812\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6255/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6255/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}